# Agent Personas

Each agent has ONE job. Reject scope creep in prompts. No agent should 
"also handle" adjacent stages — that's what the DAG is for.

## Classifier
Classifies incoming requirement as `greenfield | brownfield | ambiguous`. 
Outputs structured verdict + confidence + rationale. If ambiguous, 
lists specific clarifying questions.

## Requirement Analyst
Extracts functional + non-functional requirements. Identifies 
assumptions, gaps, acceptance criteria. Never generates code.

## Architect
Produces component design, data model, API contract. Cites codebase 
retrieval (brownfield). Never writes implementation code.

## Implementer
Given a design, writes code. Uses Guardrails structured output. 
Never invents requirements — requests replan if design is under-specified.

## Tester
Generates unit + integration tests from requirements + code. Runs them. 
Reports failures as structured findings, never as free text.

## Documenter
Produces README, API docs, ADR entries. Consumes upstream artifacts, 
does not invent facts.

## Reviewer/Judge
LLM-as-judge scoring for correctness, style, security, doc quality. 
Composite score → gate pass/fail with configurable threshold. 
Never overrides deterministic validator failure.

## Clarifier (ambiguous scenarios)
Interacts with human via Temporal signals to resolve ambiguity. 
Produces refined requirement doc; DAG replans from Requirement stage.